    "body": "# Bug report\n\n### Bug description:\n\nLeakSanitizer detects memory leaks when running `test_capi` with refleak detection. The leaks occur during subinterpreter creation via `Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig()`.\n\n## Affected Versions\n\n- Python 3.12\n- Python 3.13  \n- Python 3.14\n- CPython main branch\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Build CPython with AddressSanitizer and debug mode:\n```bash\nCC=clang CXX=clang++ ./configure --with-address-sanitizer --with-pydebug --with-undefined-behavior-sanitizer --disable-optimizations && make -j$(nproc)\n```\n\n2. Run test_capi with refleak detection:\n```bash\n./python -X dev -X showrefcount -m test -R 5:5 test_capi -j$(nproc)\n```\n\n## Logs\n\n[312.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22984810/312.log)\n[313.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22984809/313.log)\n[314.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22984812/314.log)\n[main.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22984811/main.log)\n\n### CPython versions tested on:\n\n3.15, CPython main branch, 3.14, 3.13, 3.12\n\n### Operating systems tested on:\n\nLinux\n\n<!-- gh-linked-prs -->\n### Linked PRs\n* gh-140303\n* gh-140360\n* gh-140684\n<!-- /gh-linked-prs -->\n",
